{
  "summary": "This experiment tested a multimodal multiprofile model using PCA_n2000 RNA encoding, ResNet50 image features, avgpool aggregation, and concat fusion, achieving 61.9% validation accuracy (vs. 52.7% for singleprofile multimodal baselines). The result suggests aggregation may improve performance in multiprofile settings, though uncertainty remains about its relative impact compared to other aggregation methods or modality interactions, as no direct comparisons to alternative aggregators were conducted."
}

